# JurisCore server configuration — example file.
#
# If .env.local does not exist yet: copy this file to .env.local in this same folder and
# fill in the values there. If .env.local already exists: edit that file instead, so your
# other settings (model allowlist, emergency stop) are kept. Do not overwrite it.
# .env.local is listed in .gitignore: it is never committed and never leaves this machine.
# Full steps for every way of running JurisCore: docs/GATEWAY_SETUP.md

# 1. Your proprietary LLM API key.
#    You create this on your LLM provider's developer platform (for example the Anthropic
#    Console or the OpenAI platform) and paste it here. JurisCore keeps it on the server and
#    never sends it to the browser. See docs/GATEWAY_SETUP.md for the providers this build
#    accepts.
JURISCORE_LLM_API_KEY=

# 2. The gateway switch. "enabled" turns the LLM Gateway on; "disabled" forces it off.
#    Leaving it empty means: on when a key is set above.
JURISCORE_GATEWAY=enabled

# 3. The unlock phrase you type into the dashboard.
#    JurisCore generates this for you: open the dashboard, choose "Set up gateway" in the
#    header, and copy the suggested phrase here. 16 characters or more. Never the API key.
JURISCORE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# Optional.
# Provider name. Only "anthropic" is accepted in this build; it is also the default.
JURISCORE_LLM_PROVIDER=
# Comma-separated model allowlist. Default: the provider's default model.
JURISCORE_GATEWAY_MODELS=
# Emergency stop: 1 refuses every model request until removed.
JURISCORE_GATEWAY_KILL=
# Legacy name for the API key, still read when JURISCORE_LLM_API_KEY is empty.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
